    "project_description": "The Project Zone involves in Central Seram Region, Maluku Province, Indonesia of total area of 57,748 ha, and geographical coordination is -3.0893 ~ -3.4675 S, 128.8178 ~129.6464 E. Project zone is distributed in 5 sub-districts including Tehoru, Teluk Elpaputih, Teon Nila Serua, Kota Masohi and Amahai. There are 2 Project Accounting Area (PAA): PAA1: BLM_Forest ha  Improved Forest Management from logged to protect. PAA2: GES2_Forest ha  Improved Forest Management from logged to protect There is 1 Project Agarwood Restoration Area (PARA) not counted for carbon credites: PARA1:  Agarwood Restoration Plantation. CSIR IFM  project implements measures designed to protect the natural ecosystems in the above mentioned PAAs, with a focus on preventing the main drivers of deforestation and conversion in these PAAS. These activities provide new opportunities to change the agents’ behavior and include: ●\tincreased employment opportunities, and implementations of sustainable income generating scheme (SIGS) activities throughout PA. ●\tImprove the general welfare of local community with the UN SDGs framework. ●\tempowerment with local communities NTFP, with microfinance through cooperatives to convert deforestation activities to forest protection. Project objectives and activities are designed to benefit climate, communities and biodiversity in this area. The objectives of each of these components are as follows: Climate Objectives ●\tReduce CO2 emissions resulting from the PAAs Improved Forest Management  From Logged to Protect Forest of 33,989,500 tCO2e in crediting period from 15 Auguest 2022 to 14 Auguest 2047. Community Objectives ●\tImprove community welfare by Sustainable Income Generation Groups (SIGG), Creating local foods in meat/egg and milk with  SIGG, have clean and safe drinking water in  villages, equality of women, having good dental oral health, improve quality of education and gender equality, construct affordable solar energy to  villages.",
